WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.800
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 2 is out,
and so much huge stuff happens, let’s get

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.820
right into it.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.760
We begin beyond the Wall with Bran and Bloodraven,
known in the books as “the three-eyed crow”,

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.070
and in the show, as the “three eyed-raven”.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.570
Remember, Bloodraven is a sort of a mystical
mysterious tree-wizard dude, connected to

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.180
the old gods, and the children of the forest.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.730
He trains Bran to use the powers of a greenseer,
which involves warging into animals, and having

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.940
visions of the present and past . This scene
is one of those visions, it’s of Winterfell

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.220
years ago, with a young Ned Stark, Benjen
Stark, Lyanna Stark, Rodrick Cassel, Old Nan,

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.250
and Hodor, or should we say Willas, who talks.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.510
Hodor talks!

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.280
Which raises the question of “what happened?”

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.700
Book readers have been theorising for years
that Hodor might have had his mind broken

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.410
by seeing something cold and terrible in the
Winterfell crypts, or maybe, that during one

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:56.240
of Bran’s visions, he might mess with young
Hodor’s mind by trying to talk to him or

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.320
warg into him from the present.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.270
Either way, it’s really cool that they’re
bringing this up in the show – maybe we’ll

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.510
finally find out why Hodor hodors.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:08.399
It’s also awesome to see the young Stark
siblings, especially Lyanna.

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:12.260
She’s the one who gets caught up with Prince
Rhaegar Targaryen, which leads to Robert’s

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:17.789
Rebellion, the death of Lyanna and, the theories
claim, the birth of Jon Snow, which will probably

00:01:17.789 --> 00:01:22.960
finally be revealed next episode – check
out the R+L=J video if you wanna know more.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.369
So yeah, heaps happening up here, but Meera’s
pretty down.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:30.439
To be fair, her brother died, she’s stuck
in a cave in a frozen wasteland, and all she’s

00:01:30.439 --> 00:01:35.049
got for company is Hodor, a creepy elf-child,
and a couple of fuckin tree-wizards getting

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:39.960
high on greendreams . It is interesting that
this child of the forest says that Bran “isn’t

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.200
going to stay here forever”.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.360
Lotta folks thought he would, that he’d
slowly become one with the tree, like Bloodraven,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.679
cause really, where’s he gonna go?

00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:51.729
He still can’t walk outside of the Matrix
of his visions.

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:55.530
Is Hodor gonna carry him all the way back
south, in winter, to the Wall?

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:59.249
Is that where Bran will fight the war for
the dawn against the white walkers, whatever

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:00.630
that means exactly?

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.709
And can Bloodraven really be trusted?

00:02:02.709 --> 00:02:06.000
The plot’s progressing quickly, so we’ll
probably find out soon.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.440
At the Wall, Alliser and his men confront
Davos and the loyal black brothers, but Wun

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:15.410
Wun bursts in with the wildlings and Tormund
and Edd, who take Castle Black from the Watch.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:18.880
Props to this guy for thinking he could kill
a fourteen foot giant with a crossbow bolt

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.210
– better luck next time.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:24.040
But yeah, like Alliser says, it really is
an historic thing to see wildlings in control

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.610
at Castle Black – in the thousands of years
of the Watch, this has, as far as we know,

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.470
never happened before.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.530
Then down in King’s Landing, some common
bloke is talking smack about Cersei, so Robert

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.490
Strong turns up and splatters his brain on
the wall.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:42.560
The Mountain has always been scary, because
he’s so huge and violent, but now that he’s

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.040
an unspeaking, unfeeling, undead monster,
the Mountain is more terrifying than ever.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.230
But anyway King Tommen bars Cersei from going
to Myrcella’s funeral.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:55.760
At the Sept we learn Tommen did this to try
to protect her, he feels guilty, feels like

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.280
he failed her – so later he goes and asks
for forgiveness, and asks for Cersei to teach

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:05.360
him how to be strong, which can’t possibly
go well – you can almost see some Joffrey

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.470
in Tommen’s eyes sometimes.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.610
Back at the Sept, Jaime threatens the High
Sparrow, and the Sparrow threatens right back,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.880
saying “together, we can overthrow an empire”.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.400
Which sounds like a very political goal for
these religious fanatics to have, right?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.250
Do they really just want to punish sinners
for their sins, or do they want to establish

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.510
a whole new order in capital?

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.330
There are conspiracy theories about the High
Sparrow, trying to explain who he is and what

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.470
he wants, but honestly none of it’s all
that convincing.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.330
Hopefully we’ll find out more about the
sparrows in the episodes to come.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:40.460
Over in Meereen, Tyrion, Varys, Missandei
and Grey Worm have a strategic chat.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.060
Varys says that the slavers have taken back
Yunkai and Astapor, which could lead to a

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.520
siege of Meereen, like in the books.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.020
Then Tyrion visits the dragons down in the
basement, and he doesn’t get roasted like

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.610
one character does in the books, in fact Tyrion
and the dragons seem to… get along.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:58.840
Tyrion has this touching moment talking about
his childhood dreams of dragons, like a kid

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.800
talking about dinosaurs, and the dragons seem
to listen, and understand.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.240
Which reminds us how little we know about
dragons.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.740
How intelligent are they?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.080
How loyal are they?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.170
And just how destructive can they be?

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.720
Now that Tyrion has unchained them, we’ll
probably soon find out.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.650
Also, this connection Tyrion seems to have
with the dragons might support the theory

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:24.199
that Tyrion is the son not of Tywin Lannister
but of the Mad King Aerys Targaryen.

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:28.000
This is a controversial theory, but it could
almost make sense.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.590
Having Targaryen blood may allow Tyrion to
one day ride a dragon, like Daenerys does

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.270
– and Tyrion does have experience designing
unconventional saddles , which could come

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.169
in handy, so – who knows?

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:43.069
Then we’re in Braavos, with Arya, and “the
waif” beats her up again, asking her what

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:48.069
her name is, cause the Faceless Men want Arya
to let go of her identity, and become “no

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:49.069
one”.

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:52.540
The waif leaves, and Jaqen H’ghar appears
– or, more likely, “the waif” wearing

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.930
Jaqen’s face.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:58.319
Remember last season someone who seemed to
be Jaqen drank poison and died, then the waif

00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:02.699
wore Jaqen’s face, showing that any Faceless
Man can be Jaqen, because the Faceless Men

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:07.990
are “no one”, they have no personal identity,
but anyway Arya’s told that her time as

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.810
a beggar is done, and she’s to take on a
new identity – probably Mercy, the girl

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.199
who works in a theatre troupe.

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:17.879
At Winterfell, Walda gives birth to a son.

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:22.150
Since Ramsay is a bastard, this baby boy is
ahead of Ramsay in the line of succession,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:27.220
so Ramsay stabs his father, and murders his
step-mother, and his newborn baby half-brother,

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:31.949
with dogs – as though Ramsay could possibly
be hated any more than he already is.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:35.560
It is a little surprising that Roose goes
down so easily – cause in the books, at

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.889
least, Roose is pretty good at manipulating
and controlling his monstrous bastard, but

00:05:39.889 --> 00:05:42.599
here, he seems to get totally caught off guard.

00:05:42.599 --> 00:05:45.240
Regardless, Ramsay’s in charge at Winterfell
now.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:50.240
We see he has the support of the Karstarks,
and also mentions the Manderleys, and the

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.240
Umbers.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.180
The Umbers are based at Last Hearth, and that’s
where Osha takes Rickon all those seasons

00:05:54.180 --> 00:06:02.100
ago, so maybe the Umbers will give the Boltons
Rickon as a hostage.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.529
We also hear Ramsay’s plan to attack Castle
Black to catch Sansa and kill Jon.

00:06:06.529 --> 00:06:10.469
He thinks it’s gonna be easy, but what he
doesn’t know is that wildlings and a giant

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:12.849
now guard Castle Black.

00:06:12.849 --> 00:06:16.620
Somewhere near Winterfell, Sansa, Theon, Brienne
and Pod chill in the snow.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.219
Brienne tells Sansa about when she saw Arya,
which is the first Sansa’s heard of her

00:06:20.219 --> 00:06:21.720
sister since, like…

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.720
Season 1.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.870
Brienne doesn’t mention that Arya was with
the Hound, which would be interesting for

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.850
Sansa since she’s tangled with Sandor before.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:32.180
Sansa says she should have gone with Brienne
when she had the chance, last season, which

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:36.910
she really, really should have, and then Sansa
talks with Theon about the guilt he feels

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.250
for his crimes – he’s still very much
a broken man here.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:46.009
While Brienne takes Sansa to the Wall, Theon
decides to head home – to the Iron Islands.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:51.160
At the Iron Islands, we finally see Yara’s
father Balon Greyjoy, the winner of the War

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.529
of the Five Kings basically because everyone
else forgot about him.

00:06:54.529 --> 00:06:58.810
Like Yara says, Balon really should quit while
he’s ahead, but the fool seems set on invading

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.129
the north again.

00:07:00.129 --> 00:07:04.529
Then Balon bumps into his long lost brother
Euron Greyjoy, the Crow’s Eye, a notorious

00:07:04.529 --> 00:07:09.289
pirate, schemer, and madman, who declares
he wants to rule, and throws Balon off a bridge

00:07:09.289 --> 00:07:10.790
to his death below.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.150
In the books, this may have gone differently
– it’s hinted that Euron may have hired

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:18.069
a Faceless Man like Jaqen or the waif to kill
Balon , which is connected to all sorts of

00:07:18.069 --> 00:07:22.159
other crazy theories about dragon eggs and
Valyria – we’ll talk about this in an

00:07:22.159 --> 00:07:23.529
upcoming video.

00:07:23.529 --> 00:07:27.949
But anyway, King Balon is finally dead, which
means the Iron Islands needs a new king.

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:32.150
Yara is Balon’s chosen heir, which could
make her the first ever female ruler of the

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.150
ironborn.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:37.080
But Yara’s other uncle Aeron tells her that
they’re gonna hold a Kingsmoot, a sort of

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.659
an election, to choose the next king.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:45.470
Euron will be a candidate, he’s the crazy
big-talking outsider , while Yara is a relatively

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:49.389
sensible candidate who hopes to be the first
ever woman in power , and in the books there

00:07:49.389 --> 00:07:54.660
are other candidates, including one with a
truly inspiring but possibly unrealistic utopic

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.660
vision.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.180
Anyway, back at the Wall, Melisandre’s still
a wreck.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.479
She’s lost her faith, and is deeply depressed.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:04.469
She’s wearing furs to keep herself warm,
which is a big deal cause previously the cold

00:08:04.469 --> 00:08:12.529
never bothered her , her faith and inner fire
kept her warm.

00:08:12.529 --> 00:08:16.590
So she’s really in a bad place, but Davos
comes and gives her a pep talk, and Mel agrees

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:21.680
to try to resurrect Jon, who looks sexier
as a corpse than most men do living.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.600
Readers have been waiting for this moment
for almost five years, and they’ve often

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.120
imagined the resurrection as something big
and dramatic and magical, involving blood

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.709
sacrifice or a burning pyre or weirwoods or
white walkers, so it’s surprising that all

00:08:33.709 --> 00:08:36.300
it took in the end was a spongebath and a
haircut.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:39.680
It’ll almost certainly be very different
in the books, but this way kinda makes sense

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:44.130
too – it’s very similar to how Thoros
of Myr first resurrects Beric Dondarrion – Thoros

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:48.450
didn’t have much faith, but he says some
prayers anyway, and Beric rises from the dead.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:52.600
But the thing about Beric is that when he’s
resurrected, he loses parts of himself, bits

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:54.710
of his identity and memories.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:58.600
George Martin, the author of the books, says
when his characters are resurrected they’re

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.570
“worse for wear”, “In some ways” “not
even the same characters anymore”, they’ve

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.740
“changed or transformed, and they’ve lost
something”.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:10.399
It’s also implied that this gets worse the
longer the body’s left dead before resurrection.

00:09:10.399 --> 00:09:13.750
So at least in the books, we should expect
Jon to be a changed man.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:18.270
But the show might wanna keep things simple
and make Jon than same Snow we know and love,

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:22.820
either way, Jon Snow is back – this could
be a fulfilment of the prophecy of Azor Ahai,

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:26.441
he could be the champion of the Lord of Light,
prophesied to fight against the walkers and

00:09:26.441 --> 00:09:31.420
the wights, he’s freed from his Watch vows
now, so if R+L=J is true, he could be crowned

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:36.110
as the rightful King – and at the very least
we can expect Jon to ride south against the

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:41.630
Boltons, perhaps to embrace his identity not
just as a Watchman, or a Snow, but as a Stark.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:47.870
We’re just two episodes into Season 6 and
so much huge stuff has already happened.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.589
Bran’s getting visions of the past, wildlings
have taken the Wall, Jaime and Sparrows are

00:09:51.589 --> 00:09:56.190
clashing and Robert Strong is on the loose,
the dragons are free in Meereen, Arya is taking

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:00.740
a new role in Braavos, Ramsay takes control
at Winterfell, Brienne and Sansa head north

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.569
while Theon heads home to the Iron Islands,
where Euron arrives and the stage is set for

00:10:04.569 --> 00:10:10.010
an election, and at Castle Black, Jon is back,
and the setup is in place for his true parentage

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.010
to be revealed.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:15.980
We’re really starting to pass the books
now, which means anything could happen.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:19.960
If you wanna know about Jon’s true parentage,
check out the R+L=J video, if you wanna know

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:23.560
about the Tyrion Targaryen theory, check that
video out, and if you want to hear the word

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.530
Hodor for two and a half minutes, watch the
Hodor video.

